    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "First win",
          "heading": "Jake White's Fiji edge Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win",
          "body": "Saturday's Round 6 meeting at the Bluenergy Stadium in Udine closed the pool stage for both sides. White's men arrived winless, having faded after half-time in a 43-15 defeat by Ireland, a pattern the Italian federation said had recurred through the tournament. Italy were disrupted before kickoff: tighthead Simone Ferrari injured his left arm an hour out, so Marco Riccioni was promoted from the bench and Ion Neculai took the No. 18 shirt."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record win",
          "heading": "Henry Slade opens scoring as England rout All Blacks by record margin",
          "body": "Fin Smith's grubber put Slade over after four minutes of Saturday's 37-12 win at Allianz Stadium, and further tries from Jack van Poortvliet and Ben Earl had England 19-0 up after 36 minutes. Ollie Chessum smashed over for the fourth soon after the restart, all without winger Tommy Freeman, an injury withdrawal before kick-off. Planet Rugby notes the 25-point margin eclipses England's 38-21 win of 2012; the Guardian calls it New Zealand's heaviest defeat by any northern hemisphere nation."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win",
          "body": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Stade de France tribute",
          "heading": "French federation arranges Aramburu tribute, Antoine Dupont to escort his son",
          "body": "The Fédération française de rugby organised a tribute for Saturday's France-Argentina match at the Stade de France to Federico Martin Aramburu, the former Argentina player well known in the French championship in the early 2000s. He was murdered in Paris in 2022 by two far-right activists, sentenced to 26 and 19 years. Supporters were to hold a minute's applause. According to the FFR, his son would walk out in an Argentina shirt, holding the hands of Antoine Dupont and Julian Montoya, honouring his dual nationality."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Farrell's jibe",
          "heading": "Andy Farrell asks if suspended Rassie Erasmus was 'drinking whiskey' on livestream",
          "body": "Ireland's head coach had the last laugh after Saturday's 20-17 win over South Africa. Rassie Erasmus, suspended by World Rugby over his comments about match officials, missed the game and instead hosted a livestream from the team hotel, open only to registered viewers aged 18 and over. Asked about it at his post-match press conference, Farrell laughed: \"Then why was it 18 and over then? Was he drinking whiskey or something?!\" He added that the Springboks later joined Ireland's dressing room for a beer."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ]
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Quesada says wing injuries pushed Capuozzo wide to start Miotti against Fiji",
          "body": "Domingo Miotti was named at fly-half for Saturday's 16-21 defeat by Fiji in Udine after Gonzalo Quesada chose not to ease him in from the bench. At Thursday's team announcement, Quesada said he had weighed Paolo Garbisi or Tommaso Allan at 10, with Miotti among the replacements and Ange Capuozzo at full-back, but injuries to wingers — Lynagh, Faissal, Pani and Trulla — made shifting Capuozzo wide, with Allan at full-back, the better fit. He added that debuting a key-position player from the start is, paradoxically, easier."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "OnRugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Back-row breakout",
          "heading": "Liam McConnell scores hat-trick on third Scotland appearance in Japan rout",
          "body": "The 22-year-old Edinburgh back-rower ran in all three tries before the hour of Saturday's 67-5 Nations Championship win over Japan at Murrayfield. BBC Scotland's Tom English noted the frustration among his supporters at his lack of Scotland opportunities. His second try came early in the second half from Darcy Graham's kick-and-chase and offload. Graham matched him with a hat-trick of his own, taking his Scotland try record to 41 in an 11-try afternoon."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Haka answer",
          "heading": "Wales haka response draws 1.1 million YouTube views in six days",
          "body": "The Dragon's breath effect that met the haka in Cardiff had been a year in the making, El-Balad reports, built to answer the ritual with something theatrical and unmistakably Welsh. ITV's footage of it drew 1.1 million hits on YouTube inside six days. The same piece contrasts it with Twickenham, where England fans were expected to try to drown out the haka with Swing Low, Sweet Chariot — a familiar tactic, it argues, beside a one-off show that took time, planning and imagination."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ]
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Edwards factor",
          "heading": "Shaun Edwards brought Pumas defence to Saint-Denis against France side he coached",
          "body": "Edwards spent six years running France's defence until the French federation ended his contract before the summer. Rugbyrama's Nicolas Zanardi doubted he had dropped his core principles for Saturday's Nations Championship meeting at the Stade de France: a 13-man first line, 14 inside the last 20 metres, double tackles to kill offloads and no easy rucks. France lineout coach Laurent Sempéré said in the week that both sides had evolved, Edwards included, as he adapted to new colleagues. Zanardi pointed to flaws France know well, notably forward circulation after lineouts."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Cardiff selection",
          "heading": "Harry Wilson captained Wallabies in Cardiff with Carter Gordon at fly-half",
          "body": "Australia named Wilson at No. 8 for Saturday's round-six Nations Championship test against Wales at the Principality Stadium, with Gordon outside Ryan Lonergan. Fraser McReight was among the replacements on a five-three bench, leaving Carlo Tizzano at openside and Rob Valetini on the blindside. Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii and Len Ikitau formed the midfield behind a front row of Isaac Kailea, Brandon Paenga-Amosa and Taniela Tupou. Wales came in off their first win over New Zealand in 73 years, and France's Luc Ramos refereed."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England rout All Blacks 37-12 by record margin",
          "body": "Fiji beat Italy 21-16 for first Nations Championship win. Scotland beat Japan 67-5 as Liam McConnell scores hat-trick."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "edition": "Sunday 22 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline",
          "heading": "Takuro Matsunaga scores Japan's lone try; Harada and Stolberg sin-binned at Murrayfield",
          "body": "Saturday's 67-5 defeat had one bright moment for Japan. In the 53rd minute a Scotland box kick bounced awkwardly past Kyle Rowe, and Takuro Matsunaga took an unconverted try, the visitors' only points. Planet Rugby reports that discipline then frayed late on. Mamoru Harada was yellow-carded for a 69th-minute hip drop, and Michael Stolberg for an early tackle in the 79th. Eddie Jones had made wholesale changes after the England defeat, fielding what the BBC called a severely weakened team."
